{"review_id": "R2HP6D7UUZYHKV", "asin": "B0CXJDDJ9X", "review_rating": "5.0", "review_title": "Amazing, professional drone results compared to hobby drones", "review_body": "Technology advances fast. Just five years ago this would have been a $1500 professional grade drone. To think you can get pro-quality performance, excellent stability in light to moderate breeze, stunning images, and good flight time for under $300 is surprising. The image is from my first flight with zero training and default settings. Videos are smooth and crisp.

Unboxing though initial setup is frankly daunting, but the in-app walkthrough is clear and unhurried and I went from inatalling the DJI Fly app to flying in under 20 minutes. Flight controls are legendary. The Cine setting is solid stability like a vintage Rolls Royce, while Sport mode is an exciting FPS experience that was just outside my comfort zone with my limited experience but I never felt out of control and frantic the way inexpensive hobby drones do. I haven't ended scratched the surface of the settings menu, but for what I need for Youtube content creation and scenic b-roll this works perfectly. It's also compact enough to slip into my hydration pack for capturing my motorcycle rides. I wish I'd bought this sooner!

One note about the connector cables for iPhone users! If your phone is in a heavy duty case, it will still fit in the phone holder, but the connector may not seat properly due to the small lip molded into the connection cable. No problem, a Lighting extender adapter works just fine.", "review_date": "Reviewed in the United States on June 15, 2026"}

{"review_id": "R1ULCHJVJ7TTQS", "asin": "B0F6Y9PB64", "review_rating": "5.0", "review_title": "Fun with roadtrip", "review_body": "I brought this 4K drone on a road trip just to have some fun with my family, and it turned out to be super easy to set up—nothing complicated at all.

Once we started using it, it worked really well and was smooth to fly. It even has lights on it, so when it got dark, it looked really beautiful in the sky.

Honestly, it made the trip even more fun.", "review_date": "Reviewed in the United States on June 22, 2026"}

{"review_id": "R1DWQ16T5GKLEV", "asin": "B0D2B25YQQ", "review_rating": "5.0", "review_title": "Best Beginner Drone I’ve Tried So Far", "review_body": "I’ve been playing with this drone for a little over a week now, and I’m really impressed with how fun and easy it is to use. The 4K camera captures surprisingly clear and stable footage for its size, and the wide 130° lens gives a great aerial view. The brushless motor makes it fly smoothly and quietly, and it handles wind better than I expected.

Setup was quick and everything connected easily through WiFi, and the voice and gesture controls actually work pretty well! The foldable design makes it super convenient to carry around, and having two batteries is a huge plus since it doubles my flight time.

Overall, it’s a perfect drone for beginners and even for adults who just want something reliable and fun to fly. Definitely worth it!", "review_date": "Reviewed in the United States on October 21, 2025"}

{"review_id": "ROHV955NE3K5S", "asin": "B0FC69FCKH", "review_rating": "4.0", "review_title": "Great as a proper first time drone", "review_body": "The drone shipped promptly and arrived in its case inside a box perfect to give as a gift. The drone comes with its own secure case, the remote, spare blades, and one battery. It does have instructions on how to get your drone up and running, but it is simpler if you can find an online video. The drone is well made, it does weigh more than 0.55 pounds, which does put in the class of needing a Remote ID. The drone works better with iOS, than with android, but the android still works. It comes with a 4K camera with some stability built-in, but it is not perfect.

The drone does come with the standard hover and home functions, but it does supply additional Blades in case you hit something. The important thing to remember is you have to do an online class and register your drone with the FAA and have a Remote ID when you operating this drone as it weighs more than the 0.55 pound requirement. This drone comes with only one battery ,I would’ve preferred to have received two batteries. I did find additional batteries from a store called DEERC that had the specific battery that will fit this drone.

There are many drones on the market at varying prices with varying abilities and this drone gives you all that you will need as a first time drone operator at a typical cost for drones.", "review_date": "Reviewed in the United States on September 19, 2025"}

{"review_id": "R3Q10ND5WU1A3F", "asin": "B0BL3NZT5D", "review_rating": "5.0", "review_title": "Amazing video - much easier to fly than anticipated", "review_body": "Amazing product. The video looks professional and flying the drone is much easier than expected. After a test flight, was able to get the drone up and get some aerial video that looked amazing!!

The remote with the screen was much easier than having to sacrifice the phone with the other remote.

The 249g size is important for both here and in Europe (planning a vacation) to get around many of the regulations on flying.", "review_date": "Reviewed in the United States on July 30, 2026"}

{"review_id": "R191XGRHFJDAHO", "asin": "B0DKJJK4XK", "review_rating": "5.0", "review_title": "This is the best drone, from the best company, when all things are considered.", "review_body": "This is a most awesome drone! I went with Potensic over DJI primarily for the price. For example, what do you get with the DJI Mini 4K that you don't get with the Potensic ATOM 2? Perhaps waypoints, but that is not enough to justify the higher cost of the DJI product. It turns out to have been a good decision, as DJI will most likely be banned for sale in the US anyway.

This was bought as a replacement for my original ATOM 2 drone which, unfortunately, was stuck in a tree for six months. The original drone finally fell out of the tree and my brother sent it to me. I was shocked at the build quality of the drone itself. All I had to replace was one set of props, on the port side forward arm. The battery, however, was completely dead, as it wasn't able to be charged to far too long a period of time. On a side note, in an unrelated event, Potensic has offered to send me a new ATOM 2 battery. As is the case with the new controller, Potensic really seems to listen to its users.

For these reasons, I would highly recommend Potensic drones to anyone. Not only are they built extremely well, the company is extremely responsive to its customers. Now it only they offered a drone with obstacle avoidance and waypoints, the DJI holdouts would probably make the switch.", "review_date": "Reviewed in the United States on November 8, 2025"}

{"review_id": "R14Q1AXNTQ3NZ7", "asin": "B0DKJJK4XK", "review_rating": "5.0", "review_title": "Amazing Drone", "review_body": "edit: after speaking with support, all issues have been resolved.

Great camera sensor, easy flight controls, all features present, and a fair price point. About the best drone you can get for the price, and support does a good job reaching out regarding any issues.

Support is on a different time zone so please allow them time if you do reach out. They were nothing but kind and pleasant to hear from each time.", "review_date": "Reviewed in the United States on September 9, 2025"}

{"review_id": "R1IEH7ZB6I1VNE", "asin": "B0BL3T49JF", "review_rating": "5.0", "review_title": "Great for photography/ videography", "review_body": "This is an AMAZING drone. Video and picture quality is unreal. I couldn’t be happier with my DJI Mini 3. This is actually my first drone and I got it for an add on to wedding packages. (I’m a photographer) This drone strikes the perfect balance between being compact enough to take anywhere and powerful enough to capture smooth, professional-looking footage. It’s incredibly easy to fly, even as someone who’s not a professional pilot.😂😂 The controls are intuitive, and the drone feels stable even in light winds. I’ve flown it around houses and open fields, and it handles both with confidence. The return-to-home feature gives me peace of mind, especially when I’m flying further out.

CONS: Battery life from what I’ve used is not the best. I can get about a good 30 minutes of use before it needs to be charged again.

I included a video of me flying it around my parents house. I did edit it in Lightroom to give it that cinematic look. Enjoy!", "review_date": "Reviewed in the United States on September 26, 2025"}

{"review_id": "R1C0GTWGYL3ZYS", "asin": "B0B91W4Y4P", "review_rating": "1.0", "review_title": "Do NOT overlook its 3-star rating! $5 Mini Spinners have better control than this garbage!", "review_body": "It won’t fly straight at all! Every launch goes up and to the side, erratically until it crashes into something. No amount of training or directional control will correct this, because it’s due to being flimsy and misaligned.

Even at this lower price point, most cheap toy drones fly straight up until you interact. Not this one. It’s horribly developed and calibrated. A company selling crap just to capitalize on recent drone hype. And the reviews reflect this. Nobody has anything positive to say except it’s cheap. Nearly every one mentions it’s impossible to fly.

Trust me and find a 4 to 5 star drone, because you WILL return this one, trash it, but you’ll NEVER use it, because it can’t do its core function!", "review_date": "Reviewed in the United States on December 21, 2024"}

{"review_id": "R4YC4R3VXHRM2", "asin": "B0H4B9LH8F", "review_rating": "5.0", "review_title": "Great Value for a First Drone", "review_body": "I was looking online for a birthday gift for my preteen, and this drone caught my attention. It arrived on time, which made my kid's birthday even more special.

We first tested it indoors, and the real-time camera immediately impressed us. Then we took it outside to our driveway, where it flew smoothly and responded well to the controls. It was easy to fly, and the stable performance gave my child confidence right away.

My kid has been playing with it ever since and absolutely loves it. This is a great drone for first-time users—it's user-friendly, performs well, and offers excellent value for the price.", "review_date": "Reviewed in the United States on July 30, 2026"}

{"review_id": "R13VH56D8ZA1IK", "asin": "B086VB89L8", "review_rating": "5.0", "review_title": "AWESOME", "review_body": "So first off the drone is pretty good and easy to learn how to use. I had never really flown a drone before and within a few minutes I had this bad boy dialed in and confidently proximity flying chairs and tables in my house. The camera is alright and the real-time video feed is a little laggy which were my only complaints. (For this price point I expected much much worse so that's not a dig on the drone just an observation, this drone is definitely worth the money.

Unfortunately, it was not long before I started getting too confident and had a few crashes. After one pretty minor crash, one of the rotors would not work anymore and I could not take off. I tried changing out the rotors and re-calibrating with no luck.. Honestly kind of bummed but definitely got a good bang for my buck and was satisfied … UNTIL I emailed the company and they got back to me within just a couple of hours. They gave me some troubleshooting ideas and were very helpful. It still would not work so they replaced it with a brand new drone and said I could keep the old one for spare parts.

Moral of the story is if you buy the drone you will be satisfied and enjoy yourself and if you don't the company is great to work with and I am positive they will get you taken care of.", "review_date": "Reviewed in the United States on January 23, 2021"}

{"review_id": "R2U72HUVOI00IJ", "asin": "B086VB89L8", "review_rating": "4.0", "review_title": "Easy, compact, and fun. Great beginner Drone.", "review_body": "My 12 year-old son purchased this drone. It was his second drone (the first one was two years ago, and it was different brand altogether), and he really liked this one. He learned to flip in on the first run, and it had pretty good range. He went out to 100 yards several times. He enjoyed bringing it out on our family walks. This was a well-priced drone for the value it provided.

That being said, we were pretty disappointed that it basically wore out one month after he got it. He didn't quite use it everyday, but pretty frequently. He got about 10 minutes from each fully-charged battery, and each walk was around 20 minutes long. So he'd switch out the batteries at the midpoint for each walk.

Near the end of one session (not a walk, but a back-yard flight), the drone suddenly lost power and essentially fell out of the air, but it did not crash exactly: it seemed to just run out of juice. After a full recharge, it failed to take flight. It seemed as if one of the back motors seemed to be weaker than all the rest, rendering it unable to fly. We tried everything from recalibrating the gyro, switching propellers, etc. We even took it to a hobby shop, but we were not able to fix the "weak" motor. The Hobby Shop advised us to contact the manufacturer, but we have not yet done that.", "review_date": "Reviewed in the United States on October 25, 2020"}

{"review_id": "R21I5GM9OLKLI3", "asin": "B0CDCFGF1V", "review_rating": "1.0", "review_title": "DO NOT BUY!!!!!!", "review_body": "DO NOT BUY!!!!!!!! I took it out of the box today and went to the beach. It made me a do an update which I did but I noticed it was still glitching a little. I have bought the promax from Costco, and when it works it works great until it doesn’t. It would just hover over me and get stuck in its position luckily I had a selfie stick wit my to take it down. I read the promax was glitchy because it’s newer tech with AI.

I bought this one because of the great reviews so to no AI thinking less glitches. Well I opened it out of the box this morning went to the Beach and was using follow mode and it flew straight into the water! I previously tried emailing Hover’s customer service with no response at all. DO NOT WASTE YOUR MONEY. I’m so disappointed because when it works it works great, I was able to get two videos before it crashed.

PLEASE SAVE YOUR MONEY DO NOT BUY!!", "review_date": "Reviewed in the United States on May 22, 2026"}

{"review_id": "R27MNGRRYFUH36", "asin": "B0CFF1SJ3P", "review_rating": "5.0", "review_title": "Fantastic Drone with a Few Learning Curves", "review_body": "I absolutely love my DJI Mini 4 Pro! This drone is incredibly easy to use and delivers stunning 4K photos and videos, making it a great choice for both beginners and seasoned aerial photographers. Its lightweight design (under 0.549 lbs/249 g) adds to its portability, and the flight time of about 34 minutes is impressive for a drone of this size.

A word of advice: take the time to thoroughly learn all the features. While the drone is user-friendly, it has a lot of advanced functionality that can be a bit overwhelming at first. I learned this the hard way when I launched from a boat. As the drone's battery began to get low, it attempted to execute its Return to Home (RTH) function. Unfortunately, because we were moving, the RTH path nearly led it into a lake!

Despite that close call, the overall performance and ease of use make the DJI Mini 4 Pro a fantastic investment. With a little practice, you’ll be capturing breathtaking aerial footage with confidence. Highly recommended!", "review_date": "Reviewed in the United States on February 7, 2025"}

{"review_id": "R2LFU698SPRSB4", "asin": "B0C5T9GZQY", "review_rating": "5.0", "review_title": "Easy for beginners!", "review_body": "I can’t tell you how many drones I have quickly broken due to difficulty figuring out how to get it to fly smooth (all in the name of saving money for something cheap!). This is SUCH a huge upgrade and the photo quality is impressive. Battery life is more than sufficient! We’ve never had it run out but do recharge after each use anyway.

This is a perfect device for hobbyists and photographers alike. I love the follow feature! It functions really well, flies super smooth, and is a surprisingly durable feeling device.

Well worth the price tag and is a LOT of fun!", "review_date": "Reviewed in the United States on July 27, 2023"}

{"review_id": "R1OTK57Y5MSHYK", "asin": "B0DF7CJL6D", "review_rating": "5.0", "review_title": "Fun and easy to fly drone!", "review_body": "This drone is an absolute blast for beginners and casual flyers! The LED navigation lights make it easy to fly even in low light, and the 6-axis gyro gives it a smooth, stable feel in the air. I love the speed toggle feature—it’s great to start slow while learning and then ramp it up for more excitement.

Headless mode makes flying super intuitive since you don’t have to worry about the drone’s orientation, and altitude hold keeps it steady at a set height. The one-key takeoff and landing takes the stress out of the trickiest parts of flying.

This drone packs a lot of features into a lightweight, easy-to-use package. Highly recommended for anyone wanting to dip their toes into drone flying without breaking the bank!", "review_date": "Reviewed in the United States on April 21, 2025"}

{"review_id": "R3GILCBMP8EIVW", "asin": "B075DD16LK", "review_rating": "5.0", "review_title": "Great Customer Service after Receiving Bad Motor", "review_body": "I have purchased this set of motors twice now. The first set went towards a 9" quadcopter and those motors worked flawlessly. I especially appreciated that the motor shaft was very thick and so it never bends during any sort of crash. This did require me to drill out the hole in my prop, but well worth the extra durability in my opinion.

My second batch of motors wasn't as good, as one of the motors was dead on arrival. I did not use the motor until 2 months after my purchase, but I reached out to Readytosky through the Amazon Customer Service Chat and they send me a new replacement motor. The new motor arrived within a week of my notifying them of my issue, which was very nice. For additional information, the ad motor I received would not spin up fully when connected to a known-to-be-good ESC. It would start spinning slightly, but never go to the full speed as one would except. The replacement motor worked perfectly however.

All in all I think these motors are a pretty good deal, especially knowing that Readytosky will replace a faulty motor should you receive one.", "review_date": "Reviewed in the United States on November 3, 2021"}

{"review_id": "R3AKZ6HE496ZF1", "asin": "B0H12Y6W6J", "review_rating": "5.0", "review_title": "Great for Small Gardens and Yard Maintenance", "review_body": "This fogger is compact, lightweight, and easy to carry, making it much more manageable than larger units. Despite its smaller size, it delivers plenty of power and provides consistent coverage for outdoor gardening and yard maintenance tasks.

The tank holds a useful amount of solution, and I was able to cover my entire yard on a single fill. The fogger was easy to maneuver, allowed for precise application when needed, and also worked well for treating larger areas efficiently.

The construction feels sturdy, and the unit remains stable when set down between uses. Overall, this is a well designed fogger that combines portability, good capacity, and effective performance in a compact package.", "review_date": "Reviewed in the United States on June 16, 2026"}

{"review_id": "R21JGISMOKSU9Y", "asin": "B0H12Y6W6J", "review_rating": "5.0", "review_title": "Works very good", "review_body": "This is a very effective machine. The unit is small and easy to carry, but it puts out a strong, consistent fog that covers a good area. The tank size is enough for a long session, and the lightweight design makes it comfortable to use around the yard. The VectorClean system is also helpful because it keeps the unit running smoothly and simplifies cleanup.

For garden and backyard use, the fogger performs well and reaches corners without much effort. The stable base is a nice touch when you need to set it down. Overall, it is a solid, reliable fogger for outdoor work.

I am giving it 5 stars.", "review_date": "Reviewed in the United States on June 16, 2026"}
